.jpg/330px-Mohammad_Sabah_Al-Salem_Al-Sabah.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1955-10-10","died":null,"birthplace":"Kuwait City","parties":["independent politician"],"education":["Harvard University"],"occupations":["diplomat","economist","politician"],"wiki":"Mohammad Sabah Al-Salem Al-Sabah"},"Q109259869":{"id":"Q109259869","name":"Ahmed Nawaf Al-Ahmad Al-Sabah","desc":"Kuwaiti royal and politician","img":null,"gender":"M","born":"1956-01-01","died":null,"birthplace":"Kuwait City","parties":[],"education":[],"occupations":["politician"],"wiki":"Ahmad Nawaf Al-Ahmad Al-Sabah"},"Q12243161":{"id":"Q12243161","name":"Mishal Al-Ahmad Al-Jaber Al-Sabah","desc":"Emir of Kuwait since 2023","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Emir_of_Kuwait_Sheikh_Mishal_Al-Ahmad_Al-Jaber_Al-Sabah_in_2024.jpg/330px-Emir_of_Kuwait_Sheikh_Mishal_Al-Ahmad_Al-Jaber_Al-Sabah_in_2024.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1940-09-27","died":null,"birthplace":"Kuwait","parties":[],"education":["Hendon Police College"],"occupations":["politician","statesperson","monarch"],"wiki":"Mishal Al-Ahmad Al-Jaber Al-Sabah"},"Q16151955":{"id":"Q16151955","name":"Ahmad Al Abdullah Al Sabah","desc":"Prime Minister of Kuwait since 2024","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Ahmad_Al_Abdullah_Al_Sabah.png/330px-Ahmad_Al_Abdullah_Al_Sabah.png","gender":"M","born":"1952-09-05","died":null,"birthplace":"Kuwait City","parties":[],"education":["University of Illinois System"],"occupations":["civil servant"],"wiki":"Ahmad Al-Abdullah Al-Sabah"}},"summary":"Kuwait, officially the State of Kuwait, is a country in West Asia. With a coastline of approximately 500 km (311 mi), it is situated at the head of the Persian Gulf in the northeastern edge of the Arabian Peninsula, bordering Iraq to the north and Saudi Arabia to the south. Kuwait is geographically the second closest Gulf country to mainland Iran (separated only by a small Iraqi coastline) after Iraq. The country is a small city-state; most of the population reside in the urban agglomeration of Kuwait City, the capital and largest city. As of 2024, Kuwait has a population of 4.82 million, of which 1.53 million are Kuwaiti citizens while the remaining 3.29 million are foreign nationals from over 100 countries. In 2024, Kuwait had the world's seventh largest number of foreign nationals as a percentage of the population, where its citizens make up fewer than 30% of the overall population.\nThe territory of modern-day Kuwait has been inhabited by humans since antiquity, particularly due to its strategic location near the mouth of the Tigris and Euphrates rivers. In the early 18th century, the territory of modern-day Kuwait was under the jurisdiction of the Bani Khalid clan; then the territory became known as the Sheikdom of Kuwait in 1752 and a British protectorate in 1899. Prior to the discovery of oil reserves in 1938, the territory of modern-day Kuwait contained a regional trade port. The protectorate agreements with the United Kingdom ended in June 1961 when Kuwait officially became an independent state.\nFrom 1946 to 1982, Kuwait underwent large-scale modernization, largely based on income from oil production. In the 1980s, Kuwait experienced a period of geopolitical instability and an economic crisis following the stock market crash. It suffered pro-Iranian attacks during the Iran–Iraq War, as a result of Kuwait's financial support to Iraq. In 1990, the state of Kuwait was invaded, had a puppet regime installed, and was subsequently annexed by Ba'athist Iraq under the leadership of Saddam Hussein following disputes over oil production. The Iraqi occupation of Kuwait ended on 26 February 1991, after a U.S.–led international coalition expelled Iraqi forces from the country during the Gulf War.\nKuwait is a high-income economy, backed by the world's sixth largest oil reserves. Like most other Arab states of the Persian Gulf, it is an emirate; the emir is the head of state and the ruling Al Sabah family dominates the country's political system. Its official state religion is Islam, specifically the Maliki school of Sunni Islam. It is a founding member of the Gulf Cooperation Council (GCC) and is also a member of the United Nations, OPEC, the Arab League, and the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation.","history":"Kuwait is a sovereign state in West Asia located at the head of the Persian Gulf. The geographical region of Kuwait has been occupied by humans since antiquity, particularly due to its strategic location at the head of the Persian Gulf. In the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, Kuwait contained a prosperous maritime port city known for its regional trade.","historyTitle":"History of Kuwait","curated":null,"indicators":{"gdp":[[1962,1828110000],[1963,1900900000],[1964,2071670000],[1965,2097200000],[1966,2391200000],[1967,2441600000],[1968,2662800000],[1969,2769200000],[1970,2873640000],[1971,3880390000],[1972,4450540000],[1973,5408800000],[1974,13006900000],[1975,12022800000],[1976,13132300000],[1977,14137400000],[1978,15503600000],[1979,24749100000],[1980,28638900000],[1981,25058000000],[1982,21577200000],[1983,20871100000],[1984,21700100000],[1985,21446000000],[1986,17904000000],[1987,22368700000],[1988,20690300000],[1989,24313900000],[1990,18427800000],[1991,11010000000],[1992,19858600000],[1993,23941400000],[1994,24848500000],[1995,27187000000],[1996,31492400000],[1997,30350200000],[1998,25943700000],[1999,30122400000],[2000,37718700000],[2001,34889600000],[2002,38135800000],[2003,47874600000],[2004,59439100000],[2005,80798600000],[2006,101557000000],[2007,114634000000],[2008,147380000000],[2009,105969000000],[2010,115416000000],[2011,154039000000],[2012,174048000000],[2013,174168000000],[2014,162650000000],[2015,114586000000],[2016,109407000000],[2017,120688000000],[2018,138646000000],[2019,140856000000],[2020,111045000000],[2021,148351000000],[2022,183502000000],[2023,165463000000],[2024,160903000000],[2025,157209000000]],"gdpPerCapita":[[19